Natural operation graphs and product-sum collisions (codex-2026-05-31 S365)
==============================================================================

Operation graph collapse/sparsity
  Additive simple edge: x->z iff exists y>=1 with x+y=z.
  Multiplicative simple edge: x->z iff exists y>=2 with x*y=z.

     N  A_edges A_expected  A_Hasse  M_edges   M+unit  M_Hasse      M/A
     8       28         28        7        5       12        8   0.1786
    12       66         66       11       12       23       14   0.1818
    20      190        190       19       27       46       26   0.1421
    30      435        435       29       52       81       43   0.1195
    50     1225       1225       49      108      157       77   0.0882
    80     3160       3160       79      209      288      133   0.0661

  Interpretation:
    - Additive edges are exactly the transitive tournament/order.
    - The additive transitive reduction is the successor chain.
    - Multiplicative edges are the divisor DAG; its Hasse edges are x->xp.
    - Multiplication keeps the prime lattice visible after forgetting labels.

