  z=18: add ordered=17 unordered= 9; mul ordered= 6 unordered= 3

  The unlabeled additive edge x->z forgets the complement y=z-x.
  The labeled fiber remembers Goldbach/partition-style information.
  Multiplicative fibers remember divisors/factorizations.

Finite product-sum collision gate
  For a sorted collision a_1<=...<=a_k,
    a_1*...*a_{k-1} <= k.
  Therefore each fixed arity has finitely many positive solutions.
  After deleting q ones and calling the remaining core c,
    q = product(c) - sum(c).
  Thus 1 is a defect absorber: it changes the sum without changing product.

Product-sum collision equations
  Sorted positive solutions of x_1+...+x_k = x_1*...*x_k.
  Reciprocally: sum_i 1/(product/x_i) = 1.

