Repo bridge
  Additive graph, unlabeled: complete transitive tournament.
  Multiplicative graph, unlabeled: incomplete oriented graph / divisor DAG.
  Additive graph, labeled: partitions of z.
  Multiplicative graph, labeled: factorizations of z.
  Product-sum tuples are operation-hyperedge collisions.

  This reframes earlier repo threads:
    - oriented graphs are incomplete tournaments; divisor DAGs are arithmetic examples;
    - Zeckendorf writes naturals as independence packets in a path graph;
    - Cayley rapidity linearizes multiplication but leaves addition external;
    - Egyptian fractions appear by dividing sum=product by the product;
    - sum-product tournament phenomena compare additive fibers to multiplicative fibers.
